# Data, third-party code, compute

- External raw data is read-only. Paths come only from `configs/paths.local.yaml` (gitignored);
  never hard-code absolute paths in Python or YAML.
- Training code reads only the canonical layer under `data/canonical/<dataset>/v<k>/`; raw -> canonical
  conversion is an explicit, versioned CLI step.
- `third_party/` holds official model repositories as pinned git submodules. Never edit upstream files;
  put changes in `third_party/patches/` or in our adapters under `src/eegbench/models/`.
- Pretrained weights live in `weights/` with `MANIFEST.yaml` (url, sha256, license); verify sha256 after download.
- Heavy jobs go through Slurm; GPU jobs must fail fast if CUDA is unavailable; smoke-test before full runs;
  never run training on the login node. Never overwrite a completed run — use a new `run_id`.
